# Windsurf rules

Read `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/OPERATING.md` at the repository root before making
changes and follow them.

- Milestone-driven development, one milestone at a time
  (`docs/architecture.md` section 29; status in
  `docs/implementation-status.md`).
- Required gates: `make prerequisites`, `make format`, `make lint`, `make unit`,
  `make coverage`, and `make build` must all pass from the repository root;
  use `STRICT=1` to fail on missing toolchains and run integration/e2e gates
  when the change requires cross-service verification.
- Non-negotiable integrity rules: only the CLI, orchestrator, and glyph
  catalog may see the requested plaintext; downstream events must never
  contain expected-character fields (`docs/architecture.md` section 7).
- Pin every dependency and container version; no floating `latest` tags.
- Do not combine service languages or bypass required protocols.
- Complete required PR verification before opening the PR; never defer visual,
  integration, or e2e checks to after merge.
- Parallelize only across disjoint ownership boundaries or isolated worktrees;
  run final gates serially and keep long-lived processes in the background.
- For user-visible UI changes, verify fresh viewport captures (phone/laptop at
  minimum; responsive changes also cover relevant tablet/desktop/wide widths)
  plus the changed browser interactions.
- Do not add explanatory comments; write idiomatic, readable code.
- Never commit unless explicitly authorized.
